# NO TRAILING SLASHES on plain directory names, deliberately.
# `foo/` matches a DIRECTORY only. A SYMLINK named `foo` is not matched, so
# `git add -A` commits it. That happened twice on one branch: a `node_modules`
# symlink pointing at the main checkout broke every npm job in CI, and the
# `.scratch/` entry added to prevent a repeat had a trailing slash and did not.
# A bare name matches a file, a directory and a symlink alike, which is what
# every entry below actually wants. Globs and the `!` negation keep their form.
node_modules
dist

# Prod-only shrinkwrap: GENERATED at pack/publish time by
# scripts/make-prod-shrinkwrap.mjs and shipped in the npm tarball only.
# Never commit it: npm ci / npm install treat a present npm-shrinkwrap.json
# as the authoritative lockfile, and the prod-only projection (no dev deps)
# breaks every dev/CI install with EUSAGE "lock file out of sync".
npm-shrinkwrap.json

# MCP Registry publishing
mcp-publisher
server.json

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs
build
*.dist-info/

# sqry tool cache (generated per-index; not source)
.sqry
.sqry-cache
.sqry-index
.preexisting-doctor-index.patch.bak
.review-unit-*-prompt.md
docs/personal-mcp/socket-release-assessment-prompt.md

# Local agent/worktree artifacts
.claude/*
# Track internal skills (e.g. supply-chain-guard) while ignoring local .claude state.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
.gateway
.worktrees
.r3-poll.mjs

# Host-specific restart/deployment notes for this private checkout.
.agents/skills/gateway-restart-surfaces
docs/plans/hybrid-multi-agent-playbook-evolution.dag.toml

# Internal agent working guide — internal repo/release context, must not ship
AGENTS.md

# Local MCP client configs may contain machine paths, account IDs, and secret refs.
windows-mcp-config-with-gateway.json

# Stray pnpm artifacts (this repo uses npm; reject reviewer-tool drift)
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
.playwright-mcp
.supply-chain

# Reviewer/agent scratch: vibe writes .vibe/tmp when run with workingDir here
.vibe

# Host-local records, never committed. This repo mirrors to a public GitHub
# repo, and internal process is not product. Plans stay public and carry the
# conclusions; the measurements and operator decisions behind them stay here.
# No trailing slash, deliberately. A trailing-slash pattern matches directories
# only, and these are SYMLINKS into the private internal-records repo. git treats
# a symlink as a file, so `docs/evidence/` left them untracked-but-visible and a
# `git add -A` would have committed the link, publishing the private repo's path.
docs/audits
docs/evidence

# Review briefs and their verification records: process, not product, and they
# must never reach the public mirror. Same reason as docs/audits.
#
# The two patterns below were written for the exact filenames in front of me at
# the time and matched nothing since: VERIFICATION-R6.md and BRIEF-R6.md both
# sat untracked-but-VISIBLE for a whole round. Untracked is not safe here, it
# is one `git add -A` away from published, and this session has already swept
# up a node_modules symlink, .scratch and a .msg file that way. Match the
# PREFIX, so the next round's filename is covered before it is invented.
REVIEW-SPEC-*.md
VERIFICATION-*.md
BRIEF-*.md
*-VERIFICATION-REPORT.md
.scratch
.msg
